{{Codex|Like a breath of wind, shots fired by this multi-barrel sniper are felt but never seen by its targets. Headshots in quick succession increase the Perigale's ammo efficiency. When the Perigale is wielded by Voruna, its ammo pool increases.}}

{{Weapon|Perigale}} is {{WF|Voruna}}'s [[Signature Weapon|signature]] [[Sniper Rifle|sniper rifle]] that uniquely fires four-round bursts. Its high burst power is kept in check by slow [[reload speed]] and rather low [[magazine size]] for its burst-fire nature, but is able to gain [[Ammo Efficiency|infinite ammo]] from consecutive [[Enemy Body Parts|headshot]] hits or kills with headshots. In Voruna's hands, the sniper holds more [[Ammo Maximum]].

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*When not zooming in, shots fired will spread out horizontally with pinpoint accuracy.
*Two zoom modes:
**First zoom has 2x zoom distance and +20% critical damage multiplier, additive to {{M|Vital Sense}}.
**Second zoom has 4x zoom distance and +40% critical damage multiplier, additive to {{M|Vital Sense}}.
*Landing '''4''' [[Enemy Body Parts|headshots]] in a burst or a headshot kill grants the "'''Gale Force'''" buff, increasing [[Ammo Efficiency]] by '''100%'''. The buff lasts '''4''' seconds and can be refreshed on subsequent chained headshots.

{{Advantages|class=Sniper Rifle|
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Sniper Rifle|
}}
{{WeaponComparison|Perigale Prime}}

{{Acquisition|
Perigale's blueprint and components can be obtained from [[Conjunction Survival]] [[Yuvarium]] and [[Circulus]] on [[Lua]], whose access requires completion of [[The War Within]]; the blueprint comes from [[Rotation]] A, while the Barrel, Receiver, and Stock come from Rotation B.

Alternatively they can be purchased from [[Archimedean Yonta]] on the [[Chrysalith]], [[Zariman Ten Zero]] (requires completion of [[Angels of the Zariman]] to access) with {{Resource|Lua Thrax Plasm}}, awarded from Conjunction Survival in quantities of 3 (Yuvarium), 5 (Circulus or Yuvarium [[The Steel Path|Steel Path]]), or 6 (Circulus Steel Path) per rotation or dropped by [[Hollow Thrax Centurion]] and [[Hollow Thrax Legatus]] that appears at the end of every Conjunction Survival rotation at a 30% drop rate; each component requires 50, while the blueprint requires 100, totaling to 250 Lua Thrax Plasm.

All components can be [[Trading|traded]] between players, but '''not''' the blueprint.}}

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*When wielded by {{WF|Voruna}} ({{WF|Voruna Prime|Prime}}), Perigale gains an additional '''24''' [[Ammo Maximum]], for a total of '''48''' ('''56''' for Prime variant).
*[[Multishot]], {{A|Xata's Whisper}}, and [[Punch Through]] hitting multiple heads all count as separate headshot hits for triggering the '''Gale Force''' buff.
*When not zooming in, shots fired will spread out horizontally with pinpoint accuracy, allowing it to potentially hit several heads at once in a line, powering up the ammo efficiency buff.
*{{M|Charged Chamber}} and {{M|Primed Chamber}} will only apply to the first shot made, but Perigale makes 4 shot bursts, resulting in a state where '''Gale Force''' is applied to the weapon in a state that won't benefit from these mods.
**By using {{A|Energized Munitions}} or the [[Synth Set]], one can achieve a magazine missing only one shot, in which case all subsequent shots will benefit from the mods during '''Gale Force'''.
*Despite requiring the fewest shots to gain combo, the weapon can make it difficult due to the burst fire wasting combo after a kill (for example, 3 shots being missed if the first bullet kills the enemy, resulting in a net negative combo for that kill). Because of this, it’s best to build combo by firing at the bodies of tougher enemies while Gale Force is active
*Despite the actual fire rate being much higher than the listed rate, {{M|Internal Bleeding}} will have double effect while the listed fire rate is below 2.5.

==Trivia==
*Pergalė is a Lithuanian word that translates to "victory".
